{"tool_name":"metasnv","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"metasnv","identifiers":["biotools:metasnv","doi:10.1371/JOURNAL.PONE.0182392"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"SNV calling software","home_url":"http://metasnv.embl.de","keywords":["High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Metagenomics","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Metagenomic sequencing","DNA polymorphism"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"metasnv","home":"http://metasnv.embl.de/","summary":"Pipeline for calling metagenomic single nucleotide variants (SNVs). It was designed to scale well with the exponentially increasing amount of metagenomic datasets and is capable of handling large multi-species references.","addition_date":"2018-05-19T16:37:03Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-15T02:15:40Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:metasnv","credit":[{"email":"bork@embl.de","name":"Peer Bork","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Paul Igor Costea","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-1645-3947","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://metasnv.embl.de/tutorial.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2478"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"metaSNV","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"migle_sur","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/JOURNAL.PONE.0182392","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2017 Costea et al. This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.We present metaSNV, a tool for single nucleotide variant (SNV) analysis in metagenomic samples, capable of comparing populations of thousands of bacterial and archaeal species. The tool uses as input nucleotide sequence alignments to reference genomes in standard SAM/BAM format, performs SNV calling for individual samples and across the whole data set, and generates various statistics for individual species including allele frequencies and nucleotide diversity per sample as well as distances and fixation indices across samples. Using published data from 676 metagenomic samples of different sites in the oral cavity, we show that the results of metaSNV are comparable to those of MIDAS, an alternative implementation for metagenomic SNV analysis, while data processing is faster and has a smaller storage footprint. Moreover, we implement a set of distance measures that allow the comparison of genomic variation across metagenomic samples and delineate sample-specific variants to enable the tracking of specific strain populations over time. The implementation of metaSNV is available at: http://metasnv.embl.de/.","authors":[{"name":"Bork P."},{"name":"Coelho L.P."},{"name":"Costea P.I."},{"name":"Munch R."},{"name":"Paoli L."},{"name":"Sunagawa S."}],"citationCount":45,"date":"2017-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS ONE","title":"metaSNV: A tool for metagenomic strain level analysis"},"pmcid":"PMC5533426","pmid":"28753663","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Metagenomic sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3837"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"metaSNV","home":"https://bio.tools/metasnv","summary":"Pipeline for calling metagenomic single nucleotide variants (SNVs). It was designed to scale well with the exponentially increasing amount of metagenomic datasets and is capable of handling large multi-species references.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:metasnv/cmd/metasnv.embl.de","@license":"https://cre